# Project Context
This is an iOS app named "whatido" focused on personal tracking (goals, time, expenses).
It uses SwiftUI, Firebase/Firestore, and Swift Testing.

# Code Style
- ALWAYS use SwiftUI.
- Use MVVM architecture.
- For testing, prefer the new Swift Testing framework (`@Test`) over XCTest.
- Use 2 spaces for indentation.

# Tech Stack Rules
- We use Firestore for the backend.
- Dependency Injection: Use Constructor Injection.
- Unit Tests: All ViewModels must be testable with Mock services.
- Using Services to manage backend calls.

# Forbidden
- DO NOT use generic `print()`. Use `debugPrint()` instead.
- DO NOT use force unwraps (`!`).
- DO NOT use `@State` for ViewModel properties.
- DO NOT use `@ObservedObject` for ViewModel properties.
- DO NOT use `@EnvironmentObject` for ViewModel properties.
